  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Volkswagen ID.4?",
      "a": "Yes, through a DIMO device. The AutoPi entry lists the Fuel Percentage signal, powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel. Query it with a Vehicle JWT in the GraphQL Telemetry API, and use availableSignals to see what a specific vehicle reports."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Volkswagen ID.4 with no connected services?",
      "a": "Install a DIMO device. Once the owner shares the vehicle with you, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, then query the Telemetry API with it."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Volkswagen ID.4?",
      "a": "Yes, through a DIMO device. The AutoPi entry lists the dtc event and the Diagnostic Trouble Codes signal, obdDTCList. Read the codes from the Telemetry API, or use the Vehicle Triggers API to configure webhooks that push to your endpoint."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Volkswagen ID.4?",
      "a": "Both DIMO device entries list the idling event. Query the Telemetry API segments resource with the idling mechanism, which requires a DIMO device. Segment queries cover a maximum of 31 days."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Volkswagen ID.4 mileage?",
      "a": "Both DIMO device entries list the odometer signal. Use the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint to generate a verifiable attestation, then retrieve the rawVC through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides vehicle data for the Volkswagen ID.4 on 2021 and newer model years, and the record is tested rather than expected. The vehicle connects through a DIMO device, with DIMO LTE R1 and AutoPi listed as providers, and no other connection type is listed. DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance."
